    <briefdescription>
<para>System that provides a high-level API for building game levels. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <ref refid="classLevelSystem" kindref="compound">LevelSystem</ref> accumulates entities as they are created and records the world bounds. The <ref refid="classGameWorld" kindref="compound">GameWorld</ref> itself is created by the scene after the level is built (via GetWorldBounds accessors). This separation avoids copying a non-copyable <ref refid="classGameWorld" kindref="compound">GameWorld</ref>.</para>
<para>Each level is defined in a separate .cpp file as a function that receives a reference to a <ref refid="classLevelSystem" kindref="compound">LevelSystem</ref> and calls its methods.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classBaseLevelScene" kindref="compound">BaseLevelScene</ref>, <ref refid="classLevelRegistry" kindref="compound">LevelRegistry</ref>, <ref refid="LevelMacros_8h_1abffe427d7a82d716aaeb59f206234302" kindref="member">REGISTER_LEVEL</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
